From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nuubOS: report the core as Mupen64Plus-Next-nuubOS

The nuubOS build carries H700 patches and is bundled next to the
upstream core users can download: RetroArch (netplay, per-core
settings) tells them apart by library_name.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [nuubOS specific]
---
--- a/libretro/libretro.c
+++ b/libretro/libretro.c
@@ -653,7 +653,7 @@
 
 void retro_get_system_info(struct retro_system_info *info)
 {
-    info->library_name = "Mupen64Plus-Next";
+    info->library_name = "Mupen64Plus-Next-nuubOS";
     info->library_version = "3.0" FLAVOUR_VERSION GIT_VERSION;
     info->valid_extensions = "n64|v64|z64|bin|u1";
     info->need_fullpath = false;
